                        


Item#:  SCP-5133

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5133 is to be kept in standard humanoid containment in Site-19 (See Paraentomolgy Division's database for dietary info). It has been afforded one digital alarm clock set to the 24-hour clock as an amenity, with the alarm set to 07:00.

Items created by SCP-5133's anomalous effects are to be investigated, and, if necessary, confiscated (See Addendum 513301 for list of pre-approved items). SCP-5133 is not to be restrained from wishing for  unless for testing purposes approved by the research head of Site-19's Paraentomology Division.

Description:  SCP-5133 is a 1.6m tall bipedal insectoid entity, structured and patterned similarly to a female convergent lady beetle, (Hippodamia convergens) though it only has 4 limbs. Though wings are present in the subject, they are only vestigial.

SCP-5133 has an ability that it has described as  This ability can be used after certain events, the following of which have been observed:

SCP-5133 views a digital clock as it displays 11:11 local time. Event will fail if:

The clock is more than 5 minutes out of sync with satellite time
SCP-5133 sees the clock turn from 11:10 to 11:11
SCP-5133 sees the clock turn from 11:11 to 11:12
SCP-5133 views the clock again after looking away and it still displays 11:11




One of the hairs lining SCP-5133's antennae falls off, and SCP-5133 places it onto the end of one of its front limbs and covers its eyes with the other, and then blows air softly in front of itself. Event will fail if the hair still rests on SCP-5133's front limb when it uncovers its eyes.


SCP-5133 blows out all candles on a decorated cake in one breath on April 27th.


SCP-5133 holds out a seeding white dandelion with one limb, and the other covers its eyes, and it then blows air at the dandelion head. Event will fail if all of the dandelion seeds are not detached from the dandelion head once it uncovers its eyes.


Once an event is completed, SCP-5133 may then make a statement starting with  followed by one item, be it physical or not.

If it had requested a physical item, within 5-10 minutes, if SCP-5133 did not specify a time or place for which the item to manifest, the item that SCP-5133 had stated will manifest in a place that is physically accessible to it.

Non-physical items requested will also manifest in the same given timeframe, though the means by which they do are inconsistent across instances.1

