SCP-5133 will be able to sleep normally according to its natural circadian rhythm despite its usual problems with insomnia.
SCP-5133 will always use its 11:11 wish for this if it can.



Research personnel directly involved with the performance of Test 5133-111 on 2018/04/27 reported significantly happy birthdays during the following year.
Yearly repitition of this test for consistency in data has been approved by Paraentomology head Marie Vasquez on 2019/02/07.



A live larva, unidentified as any known species, with a body .4m thick and 1m long will manifest near SCP-5133. SCP-5133 will eat it alive.
SCP-5133 has not commented on what the larva is other than that it is its favorite food.












